---
// The privacy policy, also the App Store's privacy policy URL for the iPhone and iPad app (SITE-17).
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import Header from "../components/Header.astro";
import Footer from "../components/Footer.astro";
import { github } from "../site.config";
---
<Base title="Privacy policy · ViewSwitcher" description="ViewSwitcher's apps collect nothing: no accounts, no analytics, no tracking. Your shows stay on your Mac. The site keeps an email only if you join the iPhone and iPad beta." path="/privacy">
  <Header />
  <main id="main" class="wrap prose">
    <h1>Privacy</h1>
    <p class="lede">The short version: the ViewSwitcher apps collect nothing. No accounts, no analytics, no ads, no tracking. Your shows stay on your Mac. This website keeps an email address only if you sign up for the iPhone and iPad beta.</p>
    <p class="quiet">Updated 25 November 2026. This covers ViewSwitcher for Mac, ViewSwitcher for iPhone and iPad, and this website.</p>

    <h2>ViewSwitcher for Mac</h2>
    <p>The app runs entirely on your Mac. Your shows, views, titles and settings are saved in a folder on your Mac, and the app talks to OBS on the same Mac. When you switch from a browser on the Mac, from the iPhone or iPad app, or from a paired phone's browser, it connects to ViewSwitcher on your Mac directly; nothing passes through us. We don't run a server that your data could go to.</p>
    <p>The app goes online only for these:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Updates.</strong> It checks GitHub, where ViewSwitcher is published, for a newer version and downloads it from there. GitHub sees your IP address, as with any download (<a href="https://docs.github.com/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement">GitHub's privacy statement</a>).</li>
      <li><strong>Fonts in the starter views.</strong> The views ViewSwitcher starts you with load their fonts from Google Fonts when they're shown, so Google sees your IP address (<a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy">Google's privacy policy</a>). You can change a view's fonts to ones on your Mac.</li>
      <li><strong>An AI app you connect</strong> (Edit with AI). AI apps connect only on this Mac, and only to your show's folder. The app you connect, such as Claude or Cursor, reads your shows and views to work on them, and sends what it needs to its own service; that's covered by that app's privacy policy, not by us.</li>
      <li><strong>Anything you add to a view yourself</strong>, such as an image or a web page from the internet, loads from wherever it's hosted.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>ViewSwitcher for iPhone and iPad</h2>
    <p>The app connects only to ViewSwitcher on your Mac: over the cable, or over your Wi-Fi once you pair it. A phone you pair in its browser works the same way, straight to your Mac. The app doesn't collect anything or send anything anywhere else. Its App Store listing says "Data Not Collected".</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Camera.</strong> The app asks for the camera only when you tap Scan the code, to read the pairing QR code your Mac shows. It reads the code on the device; no picture is saved or sent anywhere.</li>
      <li><strong>Local network.</strong> The app asks to find devices on your local network so Enter code can find your Mac on the Wi-Fi. It looks only for ViewSwitcher.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Apple handles buying the app. What Apple keeps about your purchase is covered by <a href="https://www.apple.com/legal/privacy/">Apple's privacy policy</a>; we don't receive your name or payment details.</p>

    <h2>This website</h2>
    <p>No cookies, no analytics, no tracking scripts, and the fonts are served from this site, not a font service. The site is hosted on Vercel, which handles requests to it (including your IP address) to serve and protect the site (<a href="https://vercel.com/legal/privacy-policy">Vercel's privacy policy</a>). Links to GitHub take you to GitHub. The <a href="/ai#beta">iPhone and iPad beta signup</a> keeps only the email you type. It's stored with our email provider, Resend (<a href="https://resend.com/legal/privacy-policy">Resend's privacy policy</a>), and used only to send you the TestFlight invite and notes about the beta. To have it removed, reply to any beta email and ask; we delete it from Resend.</p>

    <h2>Children</h2>
    <p>The ViewSwitcher apps don't collect personal information from anyone, including children. The beta signup is meant for adults; if a child has signed up, ask and we'll remove the address.</p>

    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>If this ever changes, this page changes first, with a new date at the top.</p>

    <h2>Questions</h2>
    <p>Ask on <a href={`${github}/issues`}>GitHub</a> or see <a href="/support">Support</a>.</p>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Base>
